    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d567">

                <pb facs="0759" n="747" xml:id="pg747"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00112 EW/1–1445: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-01-14T18:00:00+01:00">January 14, 1945—6
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received January 14—4:47 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>486. For Department and Fleming FEA from Stone. In accordance with instructions
                    (reDepts 305 January 13, midnight, repeated to Stockholm as Department’s 71) we
                    have informed MEW that agreement proposed by Swedish Government as outlined in
                    Stockholm’s 136 January 12 (repeated to London as its 46) is acceptable to the
                    US Government. British concur and are cabling their Minister in Stockholm to
                    join his American colleague in so informing the Swedes. In view of above, we
                    have withdrawn request for detention of <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Falsterbohus</hi>.</p>
                <p>Repeated Stockholm as 48. [Stone.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Winant</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
